THOUGHT: The no-arg constructor initializes `tmp`, `runBase`, and `runLen` but not `a` and `c`. NullAway expects all @NonNull fields to be initialized in every constructor. Since `doSort` assigns `this.a` and `this.c` before any use, I can safely initialize them to dummy non-null values in the no-arg constructor (e.g., an empty array and a trivial comparator) to satisfy NullAway without changing behavior. I’ll edit TimSort.java accordingly.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '115,119s/TimSort() {/TimSort() {
    this.a = (T[]) new Object[0];
    this.c = new Comparator<T>() {
      @Override
      public int compare(T o1, T o2) {
        return 0;
      }
    };
/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/utils/TimSort.java
```

